    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for rust-rpm-sequoia.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 9.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "An implementation of the RPM PGP interface using Sequoia.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* sequoia-openpgp: sequoia-openpgp: Cryptographic integrity compromise via key flag confusion (CVE-2026-42784)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
